# ── Videos / recordings ──────────────────────────
# No video files in git. Source clips and every rendered animation
# (overlays, combined, phase animations, rotations, debug) are large and
# regenerable from the tracked tracking.csv — only static figures (.png)
# and raw measurements (.csv / .json) are versioned. Ignored globally by
# extension so this stays correct no matter how experiments/ is reorganised.
*.mov
*.mp4
*.avi
*.mkv
*.m4v

# ── Interactive HTML viewers ─────────────────────
# Plotly phase-portrait viewers are several MB each and fully regenerable
# from tracking.csv — treated like the animations above, not versioned.
# Scoped to the viewer dir so the one tracked week2 bifurcation HTML stays.
experiments/**/animations/phase_3d_plotly/

# ── Extracted frames ─────────────────────────────
# Generated by ffmpeg, can be re-extracted anytime
frames/

# ── Logs & backups (regenerable; phase-agnostic) ─────────
# Sidecar logs and *.bak snapshots anywhere under experiments/.
experiments/**/data/*_log.txt
experiments/**/data/log_*.txt
experiments/**/data/bulk_run_*.log
experiments/**/data/bulk_tracking_log.json
experiments/**/data/*.bak
experiments/**/measurements/**/tracking.csv.bak*

# ── Editor backups / autosave ────────────────────
# Editors (LyX, Emacs) leave foo~ backups and #foo# autosave files —
# never commit them. The leading # is escaped so it's a pattern, not a comment.
*~
\#*#

# Personal VS Code workspace
*.code-workspace
.vscode/

# ── Claude worktrees ─────────────────────────────
.claude/

# ── Python cache ─────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# ── Week 1 & 2 oscilloscope samples (large CSVs, not tracked) ────
experiments/week1-diode-iv/samples/
experiments/week2-rld-bifurcation/samples/

# ── Windows OS files ─────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
[Dd]esktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk
.DS_Store
